meta {
  name: notifications
  seq: 6
}

docs {
  In-app notifications, read back with the admin token from auth/login.
  Runs after tickets/, whose assign, reassign, request-info and complete
  requests each notify the admin account — it is both this ticket's
  requester and its assignee throughout that folder — so by the time this
  folder starts there are real, non-fabricated notifications to list.

  There is no admin-facing read endpoint and nothing to set up or clean up
  here: every request is scoped to the caller's own account already, and
  marking a notification read has no separate resource to remove
  afterward.
}
